    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d430">

                <pb facs="0601" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1948v09/pg585"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.516 Export-Import Bank/5–2148</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Ecuador
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/> No. 67</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-05-21">May 21, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State transmits herewith for the information of the Officer in
                    Chargé an agreement, signed May 12, 1948, between the Republic of Ecuador and
                    the Export-Import Bank of Washington establishing a credit of $2,720,000 to
                    finance the cost of equipment, materials and services required in connection
                    with the construction of the Quevedo-Manta Highway.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d430-f1"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d430-f1" n="1" xml:id="d430-f1-content">
                <p>For previous documentation on financing Ecuadoran highway development, see <ref
                        target="frus1947v08#pg_690">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1947, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">viii</hi>, pp. 690</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
